  "body": "Following up on the discussion that happened on [W3C Tag review on OffscreenCanvas](https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/141). There were some concerns that `commit()` was a bit of a duplicate solution for the frame rendering problem.\r\n\r\nThe 3 main issues that emerged from this conversation were:\r\n* We don't want a separate mechanism to solve the same case that `RequestAnimationFrame` solves. Current `commit()` doesn't add new capabilities and solve the same problem as RAF.\r\n* We want a solution that addresses future needs by WebXR and friends.\r\n* We want to address WebAssembly's existing code bases need for a way to commit frames on a busy-loop.\r\n\r\nTrying to solve all this, we have a modified proposal for [OffscreenCanvas animation](https://github.com/junov/OffscreenCanvasAnimation/blob/master/OffscreenCanvasAnimation.md).\r\n\r\nDetails can be found in the link, but in summary, we are proposing:\r\n* A new `RequestAnimationProvider` mixin that is implemented by `Window`, `WorkerGlobalScope` and eventually `XRSession`.\r\n* an `OffscreenCanvasContext.commit()` function that blocks until the UA is ready to start receiving commands for the new frame. This enables busy-loop on worker type of applications.\r\n\r\nThe writing is not spec ready, but we would really like to have input from @whatwg/canvas as soon as possible while we begin to implement those changes.",
